{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Análisis de Sentimiento con Reseñas de Hoteles\n",
    "\n",
    "En la lección anterior exploramos el dataset de 515K reseñas. Ahora vamos a:\n",
    "\n",
    1. **Filtrar** las columnas innecesarias\n",
    2. **Limpiar** los datos\n",
    3. **Convertir** tags en datos útiles\n",
    4. **Aplicar** análisis de sentimiento con NLTK VADER\n",
    "\n",
    "**Resultado final**: Un dataset listo para construir un modelo de recomendación de hoteles."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Paso 1: Cargar el dataset original"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cargar el dataset\n",
    "print(\"Cargando datos...\")\n",
    "start = time.time()\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('../data/Hotel_Reviews.csv')\n",
    "end = time.time()\n",
    "print(f\"Cargado en {round(end - start, 2)} segundos\")\n",
    "print(f\"Forma: {df.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Paso 2: Simplificar las direcciones\n",
    "\n",
    "Las direcciones completas son difíciles de trabajar. Las reemplazamos por ciudad + país."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def replace_address(row):\n",
    "    if \"Netherlands\" in row[\"Hotel_Address\"]:\n",
    "        return \"Amsterdam, Netherlands\"\n",
    "    elif \"Barcelona\" in row[\"Hotel_Address\"]:\n",
    "        return \"Barcelona, Spain\"\n",
    "    elif \"United Kingdom\" in row[\"Hotel_Address\"]:\n",
    "        return \"London, United Kingdom\"\n",
    "    elif \"Milan\" in row[\"Hotel_Address\"]:\n",
    "        return \"Milan, Italy\"\n",
    "    elif \"France\" in row[\"Hotel_Address\"]:\n",
    "        return \"Paris, France\"\n",
    "    elif \"Vienna\" in row[\"Hotel_Address\"]:\n",
    "        return \"Vienna, Austria\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Reemplazar todas las direcciones\n",
    "df[\"Hotel_Address\"] = df.apply(replace_address, axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verificar\n",
    "print(\"Distribución por ciudad:\")\n",
    "print(df[\"Hotel_Address\"].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Paso 3: Limpiar columnas innecesarias\n",
    "\n",
    "Algunas columnas no nos sirven o son redundantes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Eliminar columnas innecesarias\n",
    "df.drop([\"Additional_Number_of_Scoring\"], axis=1, inplace=True)\n",
    "df.drop([\"Review_Total_Negative_Word_Counts\", \"Review_Total_Positive_Word_Counts\",\n",
    "         \"days_since_review\", \"Total_Number_of_Reviews_Reviewer_Has_Given\"], axis=1, inplace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calcular nuestros propios valores\n",
    "df.Total_Number_of_Reviews = df.groupby('Hotel_Name').transform('count')\n",
    "df.Average_Score = round(df.groupby('Hotel_Name').Reviewer_Score.transform('mean'), 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Columnas restantes:\")\n",
    "print(df.columns.tolist())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Paso 4: Procesar los Tags\n",
    "\n",
    "Los tags son información valiosa pero están en un formato complicado. Extraemos los más importantes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Limpiar los tags\n",
    "df.Tags = df.Tags.str.strip(\"[']\")\n",
    "df.Tags = df.Tags.str.replace(\"', '\", \",\", regex=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ver ejemplo\n",
    "print(\"Ejemplo de tags limpios:\")\n",
    "print(df.Tags.iloc[0])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Crear columnas binarias para los tags más importantes\n",
    "df[\"Leisure_trip\"] = df.Tags.apply(lambda tag: 1 if \"Leisure trip\" in tag else 0)\n",
    "df[\"Couple\"] = df.Tags.apply(lambda tag: 1 if \"Couple\" in tag else 0)\n",
    "df[\"Solo_traveler\"] = df.Tags.apply(lambda tag: 1 if \"Solo traveler\" in tag else 0)\n",
    "df[\"Business_trip\"] = df.Tags.apply(lambda tag: 1 if \"Business trip\" in tag else 0)\n",
    "df[\"Group\"] = df.Tags.apply(lambda tag: 1 if \"Group\" in tag or \"Travelers with friends\" in tag else 0)\n",
    "df[\"Family_with_young_children\"] = df.Tags.apply(lambda tag: 1 if \"Family with young children\" in tag else 0)\n",
    "df[\"Family_with_older_children\"] = df.Tags.apply(lambda tag: 1 if \"Family with older children\" in tag else 0)\n",
    "df[\"With_a_pet\"] = df.Tags.apply(lambda tag: 1 if \"With a pet\" in tag else 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ver distribución de tags\n",
    "tag_columns = [\"Leisure_trip\", \"Couple\", \"Solo_traveler\", \"Business_trip\",\n",
    "                \"Group\", \"Family_with_young_children\", \"Family_with_older_children\", \"With_a_pet\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Distribución de tags:\")\n",
    "for col in tag_columns:\n",
    "    count = df[col].sum()\n",
    "    print(f\"  {col:30s}: {count:>8,} ({count/len(df)*100:.1f}%)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ¿Qué nos dicen los tags?\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Leisure trip** domina: 81% de las reseñas son de viajes de ocio\n",
    "- **Couples** son el grupo más grande: 49%\n",
    "- **Solo travelers**: 21%\n",
    "- **Business**: solo 16%\n",
    "- **Familias**: combinan ~17%\n",
    "- **Mascotas**: solo 0.3% — muy pocos viajan con mascotas"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Paso 5: Guardar el dataset filtrado"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Guardar el dataset filtrado\n",
    "print(\"Guardando Hotel_Reviews_Filtered.csv...\")\n",
    "df.to_csv(r'../data/Hotel_Reviews_Filtered.csv', index=False)\n",
    "print(\"Listo!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Paso 6: Análisis de Sentimiento con NLTK VADER\n",
    "\n",
    "Ahora cargamos el dataset filtrado y aplicamos sentimiento."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import nltk as nltk\n",
    "from nltk.corpus import stopwords\n",
    "from nltk.sentiment.vader import SentimentIntensityAnalyzer\n",
    "\n",
    "# Descargar lexico VADER\n",
    "nltk.download('vader_lexicon')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cargar dataset filtrado\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('../data/Hotel_Reviews_Filtered.csv')\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset cargado: {df.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ¿Qué es VADER?\n",
    "\n",
    "**VADER** (Valence Aware Dictionary and sEntiment Reasoner) es un analizador de sentimiento basado en reglas, diseñado para texto de redes sociales.\n",
    "\n",
    "A diferencia de TextBlob, VADER:\n",
    "- Entiende mayúsculas (\"AMAZING\" es más positivo que \"amazing\")\n",
    "- Detecta signos de exclamación (\"!!!\" intensifica)\n",
    "- Maneja emojis\n",
    "- Es más rápido para大量 de texto"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Paso 6.1: Eliminar stop words\n",
    "\n",
    "Las stop words (\"the\", \"is\", \"at\") no afectan el sentimiento pero ralentizan el análisis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Eliminar stop words\n",
    "cache = set(stopwords.words(\"english\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "def remove_stopwords(review):\n",
    "    text = \" \".join([word for word in review.split() if word not in cache])\n",
    "    return text\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Eliminando stop words...\")\n",
    "start = time.time()\n",
    "df.Negative_Review = df.Negative_Review.apply(remove_stopwords)\n",
    "df.Positive_Review = df.Positive_Review.apply(remove_stopwords)\n",
    "end = time.time()\n",
    "print(f\"Completado en {round(end - start, 2)} segundos\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Paso 6.2: Calcular sentimiento"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Crear analizador VADER\n",
    "vader_sentiment = SentimentIntensityAnalyzer()\n",
    "\n",
    "def calc_sentiment(review):\n",
    "    if review == \"No Negative\" or review == \"No Positive\":\n",
    "        return 0\n",
    "    return vader_sentiment.polarity_scores(review)[\"compound\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calcular sentimiento para ambas columnas\n",
    "print(\"Calculando sentimiento...\")\n",
    "start = time.time()\n",
    "df[\"Negative_Sentiment\"] = df.Negative_Review.apply(calc_sentiment)\n",
    "df[\"Positive_Sentiment\"] = df.Positive_Review.apply(calc_sentiment)\n",
    "end = time.time()\n",
    "print(f\"Completado en {round(end - start, 2)} segundos\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Paso 6.3: Verificar resultados"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Ver ejemplos de sentimiento\n",
    "print(\"=== Reseñas NEGATIVAS con sentimiento más bajo ===\")\n",
    "df_sorted_neg = df.sort_values(by=[\"Negative_Sentiment\"], ascending=True)\n",
    "display(df_sorted_neg[[\"Negative_Review\", \"Negative_Sentiment\", \"Reviewer_Score\"]].head(5))\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"=== Reseñas POSITIVAS con sentimiento más alto ===\")\n",
    "df_sorted_pos = df.sort_values(by=[\"Positive_Sentiment\"], ascending=False)\n",
    "display(df_sorted_pos[[\"Positive_Review\", \"Positive_Sentiment\", \"Reviewer_Score\"]].head(5))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Comparar sentimiento con puntuación del revisor\n",
    "print(\"Correlación entre sentimiento y puntuación:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Sentimiento negativo vs puntuación: {df['Negative_Sentiment'].corr(df['Reviewer_Score']):.3f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Sentimiento positivo vs puntuación: {df['Positive_Sentiment'].corr(df['Reviewer_Score']):.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ¿Qué nos dice la correlación?\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Sentimiento negativo vs puntuación**: Correlación negativa — a mayor sentimiento negativo, menor puntuación. ¡Buena señal!\n",
    "- **Sentimiento positivo vs puntuación**: Correlación positiva — a mayor sentimiento positivo, mayor puntuación. ¡También buena señal!\n",
    "\n",
    "Esto significa que VADER está capturando correctamente la relación entre el texto y la puntuación."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Paso 7: Guardar el dataset final"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Reordenar columnas para facilitar el uso\n",
    "df = df.reindex([\n",
    "    \"Hotel_Name\", \"Hotel_Address\", \"Total_Number_of_Reviews\", \"Average_Score\",\n",
    "    \"Reviewer_Score\", \"Negative_Sentiment\", \"Positive_Sentiment\",\n",
    "    \"Reviewer_Nationality\", \"Leisure_trip\", \"Couple\", \"Solo_traveler\",\n",
    "    \"Business_trip\", \"Group\", \"Family_with_young_children\",\n",
    "    \"Family_with_older_children\", \"With_a_pet\",\n",
    "    \"Negative_Review\", \"Positive_Review\"\n",
    "], axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Guardar\n",
    "print(\"Guardando Hotel_Reviews_NLP.csv...\")\n",
    "df.to_csv(r\"../data/Hotel_Reviews_NLP.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset final: {df.shape}\")\n",
    "print(\"Listo para usar en modelos de ML!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Resumen: Pipeline completo\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Hotel_Reviews.csv (original, 515K filas)\n",
    "    ↓ Exploración (lección anterior)\n",
    "Hotel_Reviews_Filtered.csv (columnas limpias + tags)\n",
    "    ↓ Sentimiento (esta lección)\n",
    "Hotel_Reviews_NLP.csv (listo para ML)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Pasos realizados\n",
    "\n",
    "| Paso | Qué hicimos | Por qué |\n",
    "|------|-------------|--------|\n",
    "| 1 | Simplificar direcciones | Fácil de agrupar por ciudad |\n",
    "| 2 | Eliminar columnas | Algunas son redundantes o confusas |\n",
    "| 3 | Procesar tags | Convertir texto en datos numéricos |\n",
    "| 4 | Eliminar stop words | Acelerar el análisis de sentimiento |\n",
    "| 5 | Calcular sentimiento | VADER es rápido y preciso |\n",
    "| 6 | Guardar dataset | Listo para modelos de ML |\n",
    "\n",
    "### ¿Qué sigue?\n",
    "\n",
    "Con este dataset puedes:\n",
    "- **Clustering**: Agrupar hoteles por tipo de cliente\n",
    "- **Clasificación**: Predecir puntuación basada en sentimiento\n",
    "- **Recomendación**: Sugerir hoteles basado en preferencias del usuario\n",
    "\n",
    "Estas técnicas las viste en secciones anteriores del curso. ¡Ahora las puedes aplicar a datos reales!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Preguntas para reflexionar\n",
    "\n",
    "1. ¿Por qué eliminamos las stop words antes del análisis de sentimiento? ¿Podría esto causar problemas?\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Si una reseña dice \"not bad\" — ¿cómo maneja VADER la negación? ¿Es mejor o peor que un enfoque de palabra por palabra?\n",
    "\n",
    "3. ¿Qué limitaciones tiene este dataset para un sistema de recomendación real?"
   ]
  }
